+## archive-logs.sh
 
-Archives are pruned by hand today.
+```
+bin/archive-logs.sh [--keep-days N] SERVICE [SERVICE...]
+```
+
+Packs the logs of each named service from `logs/` into a dated tarball
+`archives/SERVICE-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz`. It runs from cron on the log host every night.
+
+- Several services can be given in one run, for example `bin/archive-logs.sh api web`.
+  Service names must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*$` and have a directory under `logs/`.
+- `--keep-days N` (N a positive integer) removes archives older than N days from `archives/`
+  after all the new archives are written. Only regular files named `*-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz` are
+  removed. If any service fails, the run stops with a non-zero status and nothing is pruned.
+  Without the option nothing is removed.
+- On success it prints one summary line, for example
+  `archived 2 service(s): api web; pruned 3 archive(s) older than 7 days`.
+- Exit status: 0 success, 2 invalid service name, 64 usage error, 66 service has no logs.
+
+`logs/` and `archives/` are resolved relative to the repository, not the working directory.
